  "notes": "Book Weave from PP (DanceCentral and Ballroom Guide charts) for counts 1-3: promenade, then closed as the follow closes round in front of the lead while he turns left. On 4-5 he backs the line of dance with her outside partner on 4 and closed on 5, then they open into promenade on 6: the less-turned variant the owner dances (about 5/8 in all). Provisional: her free foot drawn in late on 1 and 2, his foot pointed an eighth left on 3, and her count-5 left uncrossing wide behind her right. Usually followed by Promenade Walk and Close."
